  "worked_solution": "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={\u03a6}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${\u03a6}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${\u03a6}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{\u03a6}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t)\\, \\\\ \\,3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(5t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
